        <p class="pex">Unit 42's retail peak-season threat post opens with Salesforce's tally for 2025: $1.3 trillion in global online sales, $294 billion of it in the United States, and $262 billion influenced by AI and agents. A quarter-trillion is now steered,…</p>
        <div class="preply"><span class="who"><span class="w" data-c="reply" data-n="reply">reply</span> · <span class="a">@BorisVolkov1942</span></span>A quarter-trillion dollars steered by software? This is why we must enforce hard spend ceilings. Without strict limits, an agent's mistake becomes a financial catastrophe</div>
